# Secrets — never tracked (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY lives here).
# If `git ls-files --error-unmatch .env` succeeds, this rule is not yet in
# effect for you: an already-tracked file keeps being tracked. Untrack it with
# `git rm --cached .env` (see the README's Install section).
.env

# Virtualenv
.venv/

# Regenerable extraction/HTTP cache.
# Tests do not read this: they use tests/fixtures/recorded_http_bin and
# per-test tmp cache dirs, so untracking it is safe for a fresh clone.
.cache/

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The Library: one `<content_hash>.json` per registered document
# (DSA_LIBRARY_DIR, default `library/`). It is a local shelf — whose PDFs it
# describes differs per machine — and it is regenerable by re-analyzing.
# User labels live here too, so do not delete it casually; just do not commit it.
#
# Leading slash, deliberately: an unanchored `library/` would also match
# `src/datasheet_analyzer/library/`, the store's own source package, and
# silently untrack it. Same for `/sessions/`.
/library/

# Design cards under a tracked corpus (ADR 0008). A card is a derived cache
# keyed by `DSA_CARD_VERSION` and the corpus it was computed from, it is
# rebuilt on demand by `load_or_build_card`, and `dsa build` retires it — so
# committing it would churn on every rules change and never be the thing a
# reader cites. The corpus itself (sections, specs, plots, pins, registers,
# search index, figures) is tracked; this is the one part of a part directory
# that is not.
/parts/*/cards/

# Saved conversations (DSA_SESSIONS_DIR, default `sessions/`). Personal
# working state, and they can quote NDA material.
/sessions/

# Built frontend assets (`npm run build` in web/), served by `dsa serve`.
/web/dist/
/web/node_modules/

# Claude Code worktrees. Each is a checkout of this same repository, so
# committing one would nest the tree inside itself.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Quarantined records left by pre-isolation test runs: 206 library documents
# and the sessions alongside them, all pointing at `Temp\pytest-of-afpim\...`
# paths that no longer exist. Moved rather than deleted, in case a real record
# was swept up with them.
/.scratch/library-pytest-junk/
/.scratch/sessions-test-junk/

# Family indexes (DSA_FAMILIES_DIR, default `families/`). Deliberately *not*
# handled the way `projects/` is, and the difference is what a family
# directory holds. A project directory mixes authored and derived: only
# `projects/<NAME>/project.json` records who is on that board, so the
# directory cannot be ignored without ignoring the one file nothing else can
# reconstruct. A family directory holds `FAMILY_INDEX.md` and `family.json`
# and nothing else — both derived, in full, from records already tracked, and
# membership is *declared* in the tracked
# `src/datasheet_analyzer/registry/families.yaml`. So the authored half of a
# family is committed, exactly as a project's is; the derived half is a cache,
# and it is ignored for the reason `/parts/*/cards/` is: `config.py` says of
# `FAMILY_SCHEMA_VERSION` that a family index "is *not* part of any publish
# cache key … there is no stale file for a version to invalidate", and
# committing one would manufacture the stale file that note says cannot exist.
# `dsa family build <NAME>` rebuilds it in a second.
/families/
